input.content:
# toolbox-emphasis-color — implementation plan

## 1. Goal

`ToolboxModel.defaultOption` currently declares the *same* colour token for the normal icon
stroke and for the emphasis (hover / active) icon stroke:

* `iconStyle.borderColor` → `tokens.color.accent50`
* `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` → `tokens.color.accent50`

Because `ToolboxView` maps `borderColor` → `style.stroke` for both the normal style and the
`'emphasis'` element state, hovering a toolbox icon (or an icon being switched into the
`emphasis` icon status by `dataZoom` / `brush` / `magicType`) produces **no visible change** —
the emphasis state paints exactly the same stroke colour as the normal state.

Engineering change: give the toolbox emphasis state a *darker*, clearly distinct accent token
(`tokens.color.accent70`, `#404c76`) so `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` differs from
`iconStyle.borderColor` (`tokens.color.accent50`, `#6578ba`). This is a one-line default-option
change; no view/render logic needs to change because the plumbing already works.

---

## 2. Findings

### 2.1 The defect — identical normal / emphasis colour

`/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxModel.ts:136-146`

```ts
        showTitle: true,

        iconStyle: {
            borderColor: tokens.color.accent50,
            color: 'none'
        },
        emphasis: {
            iconStyle: {
                borderColor: tokens.color.accent50
            }
        },
```

`iconStyle.borderColor` and `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` are both `tokens.color.accent50`.

### 2.2 The tokens involved

`/workspace/src/visual/tokens.ts:146-164` defines the accent ramp:

```ts
    accent05: '#eff1f9',
    accent10: '#e0e4f2',
    accent15: '#d0d6ec',
    accent20: '#c0c9e6',
    accent25: '#b1bbdf',
    accent30: '#a1aed9',
    accent35: '#91a0d3',
    accent40: '#8292cc',
    accent45: '#7285c6',
    accent50: '#6578ba',
    accent55: '#5c6da9',
    accent60: '#536298',
    accent65: '#4a5787',
    accent70: '#404c76',
    accent75: '#374165',
    accent80: '#2e3654',
    accent85: '#252b43',
    accent90: '#1b2032',
    accent95: '#121521',
```

`accent50` = `#6578ba` (HSL l ≈ 0.563); `accent70` = `#404c76` (HSL l ≈ 0.357) — two ramp steps
darker, clearly distinguishable on the default light background.

### 2.3 The `borderColor` → `stroke` mapping (why the option is the right lever)

`/workspace/src/model/mixin/itemStyle.ts:25-41` — `ITEM_STYLE_KEY_MAP` contains
`['stroke', 'borderColor']`, so `Model#getItemStyle()` turns `borderColor` into `style.stroke`.

`/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxView.ts:172-220`:

```ts
            const iconStyleModel = featureModel.getModel('iconStyle');
            const iconStyleEmphasisModel = featureModel.getModel(['emphasis', 'iconStyle']);
```

```ts
                path.setStyle(iconStyleModel.getItemStyle());

                const pathEmphasisState = path.ensureState('emphasis');
                pathEmphasisState.style = iconStyleEmphasisModel.getItemStyle();
```

The feature-level `Model` is created with `toolboxModel` as parent
(`/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxView.ts:97`:
`const featureModel = new Model(featureOpt, toolboxModel, toolboxModel.ecModel) as ToolboxFeatureModel;`),
so an unset per-feature `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` falls back to `ToolboxModel.defaultOption`.
Therefore fixing the default option fixes every built-in and user-defined feature icon at once.

### 2.4 Where the emphasis state is entered

* Hover: `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxView.ts:252-279` — `mouseover` handler calls
  `api.enterEmphasis(this)`.
* Programmatic "active" icon status:
  `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxView.ts:150-158`

  ```ts
            featureModel.setIconStatus = function (this: ToolboxFeatureModel, iconName: string, status: DisplayState) {
                const option = this.option;
                const iconPaths = this.iconPaths;
                option.iconStatus = option.iconStatus || {};
                option.iconStatus[iconName] = status;
                if (iconPaths[iconName]) {
                    (status === 'emphasis' ? enterEmphasis : leaveEmphasis)(iconPaths[iconName]);
                }
            };
  ```

  Callers that rely on emphasis being visually distinct:
  `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/feature/DataZoom.ts:270` and `:290`,
  `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/feature/Brush.ts:72`,
  `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/feature/MagicType.ts:146,169,229`.

### 2.5 Precedent in the codebase for "normal accent50 → emphasis accentN0"

`/workspace/src/component/timeline/SliderTimelineModel.ts:113-133` uses exactly this ramp for
its icon-like controls:

```ts
            color: tokens.color.accent50,
            borderColor: tokens.color.accent50,
            borderWidth: 0
        },
        emphasis: {
            ...
            controlStyle: {
                color: tokens.color.accent70,
                borderColor: tokens.color.accent70
            },
        },
```

`/workspace/src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomModel.ts:191-194,218-228` follows the same idea
(`handleStyle.borderColor: accent20` → `emphasis.handleStyle.borderColor: accent40`).

The pre-v6 theme also used a visibly different emphasis colour —
`/workspace/theme/v5.js:537-548`:

```js
        toolbox: {
            borderColor: '#ccc',
            padding: 5,
            itemGap: 8,
            iconStyle: {
                borderColor: '#666',
            },
            emphasis: {
                iconStyle: {
                    borderColor: '#3E98C5'
                }
            }
        },
```

So `accent70` is the ramp-consistent choice for the toolbox.

### 2.6 Dark theme (context, not part of the required fix)

`/workspace/src/theme/dark.ts:100-104` only overrides the *normal* toolbox icon colour:

```ts
    toolbox: {
        iconStyle: {
            borderColor: color.accent50
        }
    },
```

`tokens.darkColor` is only consumed by `src/theme/dark.ts` (verified: `grep -rn "darkColor" /workspace/src`
returns only `src/theme/dark.ts:22`), so in dark mode `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` keeps the
*light* token value. See §6 for the optional follow-up.

### 2.7 No existing coverage

* `grep -rln "toolbox" /workspace/test/ut/spec/` → only `/workspace/test/ut/spec/model/Global.test.ts`
  (unrelated). There is **no** `test/ut/spec/component/toolbox/` directory today.
* Visual tests exist but are manual: `/workspace/test/toolbox-title.html`,
  `/workspace/test/toolbox-custom.html`, `/workspace/test/toolbox-tooltip.html`,
  `/workspace/test/toolbox-textStyle.html`, `/workspace/test/toolbox-stack.html`.

---

## 3. Plan

### Edit 1 — required: darken the toolbox emphasis icon colour

**File:** `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxModel.ts`

**Anchor (search verbatim — currently at lines 138-146, unique in the file):**

```ts
        iconStyle: {
            borderColor: tokens.color.accent50,
            color: 'none'
        },
        emphasis: {
            iconStyle: {
                borderColor: tokens.color.accent50
            }
        },
```

**Replacement:**

```ts
        iconStyle: {
            borderColor: tokens.color.accent50,
            color: 'none'
        },
        emphasis: {
            iconStyle: {
                borderColor: tokens.color.accent70
            }
        },
```

That is: the single token reference on the `emphasis.iconStyle.borderColor` line changes from
`tokens.color.accent50` to `tokens.color.accent70`. No import changes are needed — `tokens` is
already imported at `/workspace/src/component/toolbox/ToolboxModel.ts:34`
(`import tokens from '../../visual/tokens';`) and `accent70` already exists on the `ColorToken`
interface at `/workspace/src/visual/tokens.ts:59`.

No other file has to change for the acceptance signal to hold: `ToolboxView` already reads the
emphasis model through the feature-model → toolbox-model parent chain (§2.3).

### Edit 2 — recommended: add a regression unit test

Upstream shipped the fix as a bare one-liner, so this file is a *recommended* addition rather
than a strict requirement. It locks in the invariant "emphasis stroke ≠ normal stroke".

**New file:** `/workspace/test/ut/spec/component/toolbox/emphasisColor.test.ts`
(the `test/ut/spec/component/toolbox/` directory must be created; it is matched by the existing
`'**/spec/component/**/*.test.ts'` entry in `/workspace/test/ut/jest.config.cjs:50`).

**Full content:**

```ts
/*
